{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1774127695,"nonce":"oSUI5+DSXe9PDPja0AMv3+tRj9A=","title":"Dynamic preset switching: mid-conversation system prompt changes (SDK-only)","message":"The SDK backend supports per-message model and system prompt changes via query(). This enables dynamic preset switching — changing the agent posture mid-conversation without restarting.\n\n## Current state\n- Presets are selected at session creation in NewSessionDialog\n- The preset union is computed once at query start (buildQueryOptions)\n- SDKBackend.updateOptions() can change model and permissionMode live, but systemPrompt changes only apply to the NEXT query\n\n## Proposed\n- Add a \"Switch Preset\" UI action in the SessionControls sidebar (or LivePresetPills)\n- When the user selects/deselects a preset mid-conversation, recompute the union text\n- For the NEXT user prompt, inject the updated system prompt via the SDK query options\n- Track preset changes as system events in the stream log so the conversation history shows when posture changed\n\n## Scope\n- SDK-only: channel mode cannot change system prompt mid-session (only per-session via --system-prompt/--append-system-prompt)\n- The UI should show a \"presets locked\" indicator for channel sessions\n- Future: explore whether channel notifications could request a session restart with new presets\n\n## Design considerations\n- Preset switching is per-query, not per-message (SDK limitation: systemPrompt is set on query(), not per-message)\n- Need to decide: does switching presets affect the CURRENT running query or only the next one?\n- System event format for preset changes in the stream log","files":null}]}